# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# balenthiran — James's portfolio site, balenthiran.co.uk. Onboarded 2026-10-28.
#
#   "Balenthiran should be tracked, want to get /apps on it"
#                                     — his note in Kit, 2026-10-28 22:37Z
#
# That note answers both questions the idea FEAT-IDEA-APPS was waiting on in
# ideas.beh: the site joins Kit (this file is that, so the idea graduates here), and
# /apps is wanted now (BEH-APPS-1).
#
# Read at balenthiran.co.uk@dev ccdf227. The site is a React SPA on a .NET API; the
# project cards come from a static backend/Balenthiran.WebApi/Data/projects.json.
#
#   DEFINED   — his words. Cites the note.
#   INFERRED  — what the site already does, read off the code. Cites file:line.
#               Each is `review unreviewed`, so it shows in Proposed and he can deny it.
#
# Promotion to main stays his: the site is public, and no grant names it.
#
# kit:repo jemmy8oy-northstar/balenthiran.co.uk@dev
#   BEH-HEALTH-1: where this app's tests live. Hosted Kit reads them from there to count coverage.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

feature FEAT-HOME "The home page and its projects"
  stage ui
feature FEAT-APPS "balenthiran.co.uk/apps: one page showing the full suite of apps"
  stage ui
feature FEAT-STATUS "What the site says about itself"
  stage ui


# ═══ DEFINED — his notes ═══

behaviour BEH-APPS-1 "A visitor to balenthiran.co.uk/apps sees the full suite of apps"
  in FEAT-APPS
  source defined kit.notes.md#2026-10-28-2237
  priority 2
  actor visitor
  when opens page:Apps
  then sees region:AppList
  contract "I think we need some kind of /apps on balenthiran.co.uk to show the full suite of apps" (2026-10-16); "want to get /apps on it" (2026-10-28)
  contract my assumption: it lists only apps that are live, each with its name, one line on what it is, and a link that opens it
  contract my assumption: the list is a file in the site's repo, not read from Kit at run time, so the page works when Kit is down
  contract my assumption: apps for one person (the birthday site) and the hosting plumbing are left off, and so is holiday-planning, an early idea rather than an app
  contract built (balenthiran.co.uk#30, on dev): six cards — Kit, Tracks, Earn Your Beers, Language Vocab, Snip-it, Macro Metrics — from frontend/src/data/apps.json, and an Apps link in the navbar; it goes public when he promotes the site to main


# ═══ INFERRED — what the site already does ═══

behaviour BEH-HOME-1 "The home page shows a grid of projects, each a card"
  in FEAT-HOME
  source inferred frontend/src/components/ProjectGrid.tsx:1
  review approved
  priority 4
  actor visitor
  when opens page:Home
  then sees region:ProjectGrid
  contract the cards come from backend/Balenthiran.WebApi/Data/projects.json, served at GET /api/projects
  contract a project without a page renders as a card that does not open

behaviour BEH-HOME-2 "A project card opens that project's own page"
  in FEAT-HOME
  source inferred frontend/src/App.tsx:27
  review approved
  priority 4
  actor visitor
  when opens page:Project
  then sees region:ProjectDetail

behaviour BEH-HOME-3 "A visitor can leave an email to hear when a project launches"
  in FEAT-HOME
  source inferred backend/Balenthiran.WebApi/Routes/InterestRoutes.cs:17
  review approved
  priority 4
  actor visitor
  contract an address that is not an email is refused

behaviour BEH-HOME-4 "The YouTube page presents the channel"
  in FEAT-HOME
  source inferred frontend/src/App.tsx:34
  review unreviewed
  priority 4
  actor visitor
  when opens page:YouTube

behaviour BEH-STATUS-1 "GET /api/status says which version is running and when it answered"
  in FEAT-STATUS
  source inferred backend/Balenthiran.WebApi/Routes/StatusRoutes.cs:13
  review unreviewed
  priority 4
  actor engineer

behaviour BEH-STATUS-2 "The /status page shows the site's work as lanes on a board"
  in FEAT-STATUS
  source inferred frontend/src/App.tsx:35
  review unreviewed
  priority 4
  actor visitor
  when opens page:Status
  then sees region:Lanes
